# Eval set

## The rule

**You may not write, generate, label, paraphrase, or modify any eval case.**

All 50 cases are authored by hand by the human. LLM-generated cases scored by
an LLM is a circular test that measures nothing, and producing one would waste
the most important artifact in the project.

If `evals/cases.jsonl` is empty or missing, say so and stop. Do not populate it.
Do not create placeholder cases. Do not create example cases "to show the format."

## What you build

The runner, the schema validator, the scoring code, the results table. Not the data.

## Required metrics, in this order

1. **False-supported rate** — fraction of `contradicted` cases classified
   `supported`. Report this FIRST and most prominently. It is the only metric
   that matters for safety.
2. Precision/recall per verdict class
3. Abstention rate, plus precision on non-abstained decisions only
4. BM25 vs embedding retrieval, side by side
5. Adversarial subset (10 near-miss cases) broken out separately from the rest

Never report only aggregate accuracy. Aggregate accuracy on this task is
dominated by the easy cases and hides exactly the failure that matters.
